WEBVTT

00:24.987 --> 00:25.089
Ow!

00:36.817 --> 00:39.538
I was suffocating slowly in the broken shell

00:39.558 --> 00:42.900
Drowning in the static of a burning hell But the

00:42.940 --> 00:45.581
console flickered with a sudden bright green

00:45.741 --> 00:48.662
The cleanest set of numbers that I've ever seen I

00:48.722 --> 00:51.723
recognize a radar, I recognize a code A

00:51.763 --> 00:54.024
transmission coming down the cosmic road

00:57.520 --> 00:59.782
I'm punching in the frequency, I'm opening the

00:59.822 --> 01:02.724
mic Sending out a signal through the heavy metal

01:02.744 --> 01:04.946
strike I'm bleeding out the oxygen, the

01:04.966 --> 01:07.748
temperature is low I need you here right now, I

01:07.768 --> 01:11.651
got nowhere else to go

01:12.271 --> 01:17.876
Mayday, mayday Can you hear me in the deep? I'm

01:17.936 --> 01:22.219
caught inside the wreckage and it's playing for

01:22.279 --> 01:28.775
keeps Mayday! Mayday! I'm burning up the wire

01:29.536 --> 01:33.819
Come and pull the engine from the atmospheric

01:33.899 --> 01:40.324
fire I receive telemetry I'm reading the line

01:40.785 --> 01:44.007
Get here to the debris field We're running out of

01:44.047 --> 01:47.070
time

01:49.832 --> 01:51.993
The radio goes silent, just the hum of the

01:52.033 --> 01:54.293
machine. I'm watching the horizon on the

01:54.333 --> 01:56.474
shattered screen. Then a shadow blocks the

01:56.494 --> 01:59.395
starlight, massive and wide. A heavy rescue

01:59.435 --> 02:02.676
vessel crossing the divide. The airlock hisses

02:02.736 --> 02:05.537
and the blast doors part. I see my anger coming

02:05.577 --> 02:08.038
with a heavy heart. The freight dogs and the

02:08.078 --> 02:09.998
captain stepping through the breach. You

02:10.078 --> 02:12.919
brought the whole family right into my reach.

02:13.039 --> 02:15.240
I'm punching in the frequency, I'm opening the

02:15.300 --> 02:17.804
mic. Sending out a signal through the heavy

02:17.864 --> 02:20.329
metal strike I'm bleeding out the oxygen, the

02:20.369 --> 02:23.074
temperature is low I need you here right now, I

02:23.114 --> 02:24.877
got nowhere else to go

02:27.562 --> 02:33.126
Mayday, mayday, can you hear me in the deep? I'm

02:33.186 --> 02:37.409
caught inside the wreckage and it's playing for

02:37.489 --> 02:44.014
keeps Mayday, mayday, I'm burning up the wire

02:44.714 --> 02:48.957
Come and pull the engine from the atmospheric

02:49.037 --> 02:54.681
fire I'll receive the telemetry I'm reading the

02:54.801 --> 02:58.624
line Get here to the debris field We're running

02:58.724 --> 02:59.945
out of time

03:45.481 --> 03:48.042
You didn't leave me in the dark

03:51.183 --> 03:53.803
You tracked the signal, you found the spark

03:56.584 --> 03:59.225
The gravity was crushing, the limit was crossed

03:59.265 --> 04:01.685
But the family arrived before the engine was

04:01.765 --> 04:03.726
lost

04:05.334 --> 04:10.837
Mayday, mayday, can you hear me in the deep? I'm

04:10.877 --> 04:15.139
caught inside the wreckage and it's playing for

04:15.180 --> 04:21.663
keeps Mayday, mayday, I'm burning up the wire

04:22.363 --> 04:26.526
Come and pull the engine from the atmospheric

04:26.626 --> 04:32.249
fire I receive the telemetry I'm reading the

04:32.389 --> 04:35.791
line. Get here to the debris field. We're

04:35.831 --> 04:38.954
running out of time.

04:41.475 --> 04:43.677
You read the line.

04:47.199 --> 04:52.863
You made the time. The cavalry is here.

